Herdr is a terminal workspace manager for AI coding agents. It runs
agents such as Claude Code, Codex, and others in panes of a persistent
server session that clients attach to and detach from, detects which agent
is running in each pane and whether it is working, waiting, or done, and
notifies you when an agent needs attention. Terminal emulation is provided
by the vendored libghostty-vt library.
